# Working with the Kedro + MCP setup

Guide for Claude Code sessions in this container. Generated by `blinded_init.py`.

---

## Architecture

```
Claude Code (this session)          MCP server (separate container)
/workspace  ──── source code ───►  runs Kedro pipelines
                                   holds data/ on its own filesystem
            ◄─── MCP tools ──────  exposes results over SSE
```

You edit the Kedro project here in `/workspace`. The MCP server at
`http://mcp_server:8000/sse` reads the same source over a bind mount and executes
the pipeline. **`data/` does not exist in `/workspace`** — it lives only in the
other container. You cannot browse, read, or write data files, and there is no
way to make one appear. That is the point of this setup, not a misconfiguration.

`conf/local/` (credentials for the real data sources) is likewise not mounted
here. Pipelines authenticate at run time on the data side.

---

## MCP tools

Five tools. Load them with `ToolSearch` before calling:

```
select:mcp__kedro-runner__run_pipeline,mcp__kedro-runner__get_run_status,
       mcp__kedro-runner__get_run_error,mcp__kedro-runner__list_runs,
       mcp__kedro-runner__get_metrics
```

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `run_pipeline` | Kick off a run (returns a `run_id` immediately) |
| `get_run_status` | Poll for completion; check `nodes_completed` / `nodes_total` |
| `get_run_error` | Structured, data-free error info for a failed run |
| `get_metrics` | Numeric metrics from the latest tracked run |
| `list_runs` | Every run triggered this server session |

Runs are **async** — `run_pipeline` returns before the pipeline finishes. Always
poll `get_run_status` until `status` is `"completed"` or `"failed"`.

